+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+On a synthetic store of 5,000 records and 15,000 cues, the `SessionStart` hook
+has the following measured p50 cost:
+
+| Version | p50 |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Before `PRAGMA quick_check` was removed from the read path | No measured number was found in this checkout or its available history. |
+| After `quick_check` was moved off the read path | 2.141222 ms |
+
+The “after” value was measured on this checkout over 300 hook invocations with:
+
+```console
+target/release/muninn-bench perf --records 5000 --cues 15000 --runs 300 \
+  --muninn /absolute/path/to/target/release/muninn --json
+```
+
+This boundary also introduced the trigger-maintained `meta.fts_rows` counter and
+the `CHECK (length(body) <= 2000)` constraint. Consequently the read-path health
+gate uses recorded `quick_check` evidence and the counter, while the schema
+enforces the body cap. The unavailable “before” value is intentionally not
+reconstructed from the separately documented 9.6 ms `quick_check` cost, since
+adding that figure to the current hook time would be an estimate rather than a
+measurement.
